From: postmarketOS <bramble@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] net: rmnet: fix NULL pointer dereference in rmnet_changelink()

rmnet_changelink() looks up the real device from IFLA_LINK, which is
optional. "ip link set dev qmapmux0.0 type rmnet ..." does not send it, so
nla_get_u32(NULL) oopses with the RTNL lock held, and all later network
configuration hangs until reboot.

Use priv->real_dev, as the mainline fix with the same title does.

---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/rmnet/rmnet_config.c	2026-10-23 22:28:04.157507177 +0100
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/rmnet/rmnet_config.c	2026-10-23 22:28:04.170198121 +0100
@@ -381,9 +381,7 @@
 	if (!dev)
 		return -ENODEV;
 
-	real_dev = __dev_get_by_index(dev_net(dev),
-				      nla_get_u32(tb[IFLA_LINK]));
-
+	real_dev = priv->real_dev;
 	if (!real_dev || !rmnet_is_real_dev_registered(real_dev))
 		return -ENODEV;
 
